# The CAD's materials. G-vii task 3b.
#
# Ka IS THE GLOW, and it is why the shipped MTL could not be used as it was: every material
# in it declared Ka 1.0 1.0 1.0, and NeoForge's emissive_ambient defaults to TRUE, so the
# WHOLE gun would have rendered at full brightness in a dark cave - smoke step 13's
# "if everything glows" failure, shipped by default. Only mat_glow may have a non-zero Ka.

newmtl mat0
Ka 0 0 0
Kd 1 1 1
Ks 0.1 0.1 0.1
Ns 250
d 1
illum 2
map_Kd isekubed:item/cad_diffuse

# 342 of the 768 faces - 45 percent of the gun - wear this material, and the supplied
# material_0_diffuse.png was 1x1 and FULLY TRANSPARENT. Nearly half the mesh would have
# rendered invisible, and no gate renders a frame to notice (L41).
newmtl mat1
Ka 0 0 0
Kd 1 1 1
Ks 0 0 0
Ns 250
d 1
illum 1
map_Kd isekubed:item/cad_black

# The glow shell, and since G-vii-d the TINT shell too - one set of quads doing both, which is
# the owner's ruling ("dyeing changes the glow color too") made structural rather than enforced:
# they cannot disagree, being the same faces. Ka 1 1 1 bakes a full-brightness lightmap in; the
# mask's transparent texels cut the rest away; and neoforge_TintIndex 0 hands the colour to
# AlchemyItemColours, which reads the item's dye and defaults to the crimson the owner chose.
newmtl mat_glow
Ka 1.0 1.0 1.0
neoforge_TintIndex 0
Kd 1 1 1
Ks 0 0 0
Ns 250
d 1
illum 1
map_Kd isekubed:item/cad_emissive
